================================================================================
2+1 SCREENED SCALAR (k-mouflage/Vainshtein) — gate run
================================================================================

S = S_GR[g] + S_phi[phi] + S_m[g~, psi],  g~ = A^2(phi) g  (conformal) or + disformal piece.
The scalar carries MOND: deep-MOND AQUAL is k-essence with K(X) ~ X^{3/2}; mu -> 1 at high
acceleration IS the screening.

G1 (3 DOF exactly):        PASS by construction (2 tensor + 1 scalar), cost paid openly.
G2 (c_T = 1):              PASS -- a conformally coupled scalar does not touch the TT sector.
G3 (gamma_PPN = 1):        conformal coupling shifts BOTH potentials equally:
                             Phi~ = Phi + lnA,  Psi~ = Psi + lnA  =>  slip Phi~-Psi~ = Phi-Psi = 0.
                           PASS.
G4 (mu = 1-e^{-y}):        PASS -- free choice of K(X) reproduces any mu (AQUAL Legendre dual).
G5 (BTFR/RAR):             PASS -- standard AQUAL result.

================================================================================
G6/G7 — THE TWO KILLERS
================================================================================

KILLER 1 (LENSING, and it is the same theorem that killed CMYG).
  Null geodesics are CONFORMALLY INVARIANT. With g~ = A^2(phi) g, photons follow the null
  geodesics of g -- blind to phi. So:
      massive particles: feel phi  => MOND dynamics  (rotation curves fit)
      photons:           blind     => lensing = BARYONS ONLY
  Excluded by the KiDS weak-lensing RAR (lensing tracks the dynamical RAR to ~Mpc).
  => A purely CONFORMAL screened scalar CANNOT lens. This is exactly the CMYG dichotomy,
     and it is DOF-independent -- adding the third DOF does not repair it.

  ESCAPE: add a DISFORMAL piece g~ = A^2 g + B ∂phi ∂phi. Then photons DO see phi. But a
  disformal term built from ∂_mu phi requires a timelike gradient => a preferred vector =>
  either a dynamical vector field or a khronon. That is precisely why TeVeS carries a vector
  and why AeST has SIX DOF (PRD 110.044015). The 'minimal third DOF' is NOT enough for lensing.

KILLER 2 (G7: Cassini <-> wide-binary lock) -- and this one is DOF-BLIND.
  The lock (committed: theory_2026/york/cassini_widebinary_lock_2026.py): the Solar System and
  the solar-neighbourhood wide binaries sit in the SAME galactic external field
      g_e = 1.8e-10 m/s^2  =>  eta = g_e/a0 = 1.50
  The Cassini EFE quadrupole is Q2 ~ q(eta) a0/R evaluated at the EXTERNAL field, NOT at the
  (screened) planetary field. Any screening sharp enough to push q(eta) -> 0 at eta ~ 1.9 also
  pushes the wide-binary boost 1/mu(eta) - 1 -> 0 at the SAME eta. Verified numerically in the
  committed route1B scan: mu_5/mu_10 clear Cassini AND give gamma_v = 1.0040/1.0001 (Newtonian),
  while the registered Amendment-10 band is 1.16-1.23.
  => Screening strength is a property of the KERNEL's transition sharpness, not of the DOF count.
     The third DOF buys nothing here.

================================================================================
VERDICT — 2+1 screened scalar
================================================================================

  G1 PASS  G2 PASS  G3 PASS  G4 PASS  G5 PASS
  G6 (screening)      PARTIAL -- works for the monopole, but see G7
  G7 (EFE/wide-binary) FAIL   -- the Cassini<->wide-binary lock is DOF-blind
  LENSING             FAIL   -- conformal coupling cannot bend light (null-geodesic invariance);
                               repairing it requires a disformal piece => a vector => AeST (6 DOF)

  CONCLUSION: the MINIMAL third DOF does NOT buy the phenomenology. A conformally coupled
  screened scalar gets dynamics, gamma_PPN=1, c_T=1 and exact mu -- but cannot lens, and cannot
  break the Cassini/wide-binary lock. Lensing forces a disformal coupling, which forces a
  preferred vector, which lands on AeST/TeVeS with 6 DOF -- exactly where the literature already
  sits, and where a0 is NOT structural.

  This is not a new kill of AeST (its gates are banked); it is the statement that the 2+1 route
  COLLAPSES INTO AeST rather than providing a cheaper alternative. The 'minimal sacrifice' turns
  out not to be minimal: lensing costs a vector, not a scalar.
================================================================================
